chat_messages.text:
 Absolutely! You've identified the one genuinely interesting piece - the autonomous decision-making - and you're spot on that you can build that yourself.

**The "AI thinking for itself" part is just:**
- Context awareness (what data is available)
- Decision logic (when to call which APIs)
- Chain-of-thought reasoning (planning multi-step actions)

**You can absolutely build this yourself:**
```javascript
// Your own intelligent routing
async function handleUserQuery(query, context) {
  // Analyze what the user needs
  const intent = await analyzeIntent(query);

  // Decide what data/actions are needed
  if (intent.needsInventory) {
    const inventory = await getInventory();
    context.inventory = inventory;
  }

  if (intent.needsAnalysis) {
    const analysis = await analyzeData(context);
    context.analysis = analysis;
  }

  // Send enriched context to AI
  return await callAI(query, context);
}
```

**Since MCP is open source, you can:**
- Study their decision-making algorithms
- Copy the good parts (context management, tool selection logic)
- Adapt it to work with any AI provider
- Remove the vendor lock-in
- Control your own rate limiting and costs

**Your approach would actually be better because:**
- You can optimize for your specific use cases
- You're not limited to Claude's tool-calling format
- You can implement smarter caching and batching
- You control when the AI gets called (and billed)

The "magic" of MCP isn't really magic - it's just structured context management and decision trees. You can build that logic yourself and make it work with GPT, Claude, or whatever comes next.

You're thinking like a smart engineer: take the good ideas, skip the vendor lock-in.

